During my internship at ZeonAi Labs, I applied AWS services extensively to build scalable, reliable, and secure features for enterprise-grade applications.
My primary work involved designing and optimizing the document storage workflow for the Indian Airforce DMS, where AWS S3 played a central role.

I engineered a Google Drive–style file and folder upload system backed by AWS S3, enabling secure object storage, high-speed uploads, and efficient retrieval workflows.
I implemented multi-part uploads to handle large files and configured structured S3 key patterns to support multi-tenant isolation.
Along with this, I designed metadata persistence in MySQL to ensure each S3 object was consistently tracked, even during concurrent uploads.

To improve performance, I integrated AWS S3 presigned URLs for controlled and temporary access, reducing server load and providing secure, direct upload capability to the client.
This significantly improved upload speed and enhanced the overall user experience.

I also applied AWS best practices for security by enabling proper bucket policies, using IAM roles with least-privilege access, and ensuring strict tenant-level separation for sensitive data belonging to the Indian Airforce.

As part of the scalability work, I optimized how files were stored, accessed, and versioned on S3, helping reduce redundancy and improving overall system throughput.
This contributed to a 40% improvement in upload time when combined with optimized backend logic.

Overall, AWS—especially S3 and related security practices—was essential in delivering a robust, scalable, and secure document management workflow capable of supporting high-volume, mission-critical operations.
